                       v2redux — licensing

All original work in the v2redux repository — the C++ port of the V2
engine, the test and oracle harness, the build system, and the
documentation — is dedicated to the public domain under the Creative
Commons CC0 1.0 Universal dedication.

    To the extent possible under law, the authors of this port have
    waived all copyright and related or neighboring rights to the
    original work in that repository. This work is published from
    Germany / Cyprus.

    CC0 1.0: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

That port derives from the V2 synthesizer, written 2000-2008 by
Tammo "kb" Hinrichs, who placed his V2 code in the public domain. His
original dedication is preserved verbatim:

    -----------------------------------------------------------------
    V2 code written 2000-2008 by Tammo "kb" Hinrichs

    I hereby place this code (as contained in this directory and the
    subdirectories "bin", "conv2m", "in_v2m", "libv2", "tinyplayer"
    and "tool") in the public domain.
    -----------------------------------------------------------------

Some original V2 source files additionally carried an "Artistic License
2.0" header from their genthree lineage; the governing LICENSE.txt in
the upstream release is the public-domain dedication above. Original
notices in ported source files are preserved where present.

Only the source code is used by this plugin. The v2redux test corpus
(corpus/, songs (C) Farbrausch / .theprodukkt) is NOT public domain and
is not redistributed here; it is only downloaded as build-time test
input when V2M_BUILD_TESTS is enabled.
